# Production builds talk to the real backend. Where an endpoint does not exist
# yet, lib/api.ts degrades to cached and then to demo data, and the screen says
# which of those it is showing — it never renders fixtures as live.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://resqnet-api-0jmr.onrender.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK=false

# NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK is opt-in: anything other than the exact string "true"
# means live. That way a deployment where nobody set it calls the real API and
# says so when it fails, instead of silently serving fixtures as if they were
# real incidents. Set it to true only to demo without a backend.
